===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# [[contrarily|Contrarily]]
#: ''I never act [[contrary to]] my principles.''

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[opposite]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King Lear|II|ii|passage=No '''contraries''' hold more antipathy<br>Than I and such a knave.}}
# {{lb|en|logic}} One of a pair of [[proposition]]s that cannot both be simultaneously true, though they may both be false.
#* {{RQ:Watts Logick|passage=If two universals differ in quality, they are '''contraries'''; as, every vine is a tree; no vine is a tree. These can never be both true together; but they may be both false.}}
# {{lb|en|historical}} A type of [[loaded]] [[die]].

